## Start here: project summary and reading guide

This application is a local Bill Pay migration investigation and population-preparation dashboard. It replaced repeated manual cross-file inspection with a connected view of FIS customers, funding accounts, payees and supplied payments. It then grew to support DNA segmentation, DFS closed-account reconciliation, reviewed Finacle driver extracts and reversible Go/No-Go exclusions.

The source and package name is **Billpay dashboard** (`billpay-dashboard`). This README documents the implementation in this source tree.

There are three deliberately separate populations:

1. **Current deconversion delivery:** Member-defined customer profiles and their linked records, reduced by any applied Go/No-Go exclusions. Overview and customer segmentation describe this population.
2. **Full DNA workbook:** an independent reference of exact CIF-to-segment assignments. It can include customers absent from the delivery; it never creates Member customers.
3. **Finacle driver:** an independently supplied list of unique CIFs. Driver File Builder starts here and subtracts the union of explicitly selected exclusion criteria. It is not a copy of Overview.

Never make these counts agree by changing their denominators. Reconcile profiles, unique CIFs, account/CIF pairs, outside-driver populations and overlaps explicitly.

